%!PS
% A table without rules: its rows are cut into cells by wide moves that
% line up. Two lines with a gap each that do not line up, and two
% columns of prose set one column after the other, are no table.
/Times-Roman findfont 10 scalefont setfont
72 720 moveto (A sentence before the table.) show
/C { moveto show } def
(alpha) 100 690 C (one) 200 690 C (first) 300 690 C
(beta) 100 678 C (two) 200 678 C (second) 300 678 C
(gamma) 100 666 C (three) 200 666 C (third) 300 666 C
(A line with a gap) 72 630 C (here.) 160 630 C
(Another longer line of words) 72 618 C (there.) 230 618 C
(Left column line one) 72 580 C (Left column line two) 72 568 C
(Right column line one) 320 580 C (Right column line two) 320 568 C
showpage
